@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Driver Channels"; var refs = ViewBag.DemoReferences as IReadOnlyList<string> ?? Array.Empty<string>(); var apkExists = ViewBag.ApkExists as bool? ?? false; }
<div class="sp-toolbar"><div><span class="sp-badge sp-badge--ai">WhatsApp-first driver companion</span><h1>Smart Port Driver Companion Channels</h1><p>Core driver demo works through WhatsApp sandbox/live-test, the web driver companion, and token-secured mobile APIs. Android is an optional supporting companion, not a deployment blocker.</p></div><div class="sp-toolbar__actions"><a href="/driver/demo" class="sp-btn sp-btn--primary">Open web driver companion</a><a href="/fleet/notifications" class="sp-btn sp-btn--outline">Notification history</a></div></div>
<div class="sp-grid sp-grid--4"><article class="sp-card"><h2>1. WhatsApp</h2><p>Driver updates and location requests can be simulated or sent through Meta Cloud API LiveTest when credentials and approved recipients are configured.</p></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>2. Web companion</h2><p>Use <a href="/driver/demo">/driver/demo</a> for status, confirmations and location check-ins without APK installation.</p></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>3. Mobile API</h2><p>Token header <code>X-SmartPort-Mobile-Token</code> protects truck status, notifications, confirmations and location check-ins.</p></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>4. Optional Android</h2><p>Native Kotlin source exists at <code>mobile/SmartPortDriverCompanion</code> and can be built through GitHub Actions or Android Studio.</p></article></div>
<div class="sp-grid sp-grid--2"><article class="sp-card sp-premium-panel"><h2>Companion capabilities</h2><ul class="sp-checklist"><li>Fetches truck status from <code>/api/mobile/truck/status/{reference}</code></li><li>Shows queue number, ETA, gate, staging zone, status and latest instruction</li><li>Shows backend notification history</li><li>Posts confirmations, driver commands and demo location check-ins</li><li>Calls backend Copilot endpoint; it stores no Gemini or WhatsApp secrets</li><li>Reference for judging: <code>SPQ-2026-0042</code></li><li>Demo code: <code>culltron-driver-2026</code></li></ul></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>Backend URLs</h2><dl class="driver-dl"><dt>Default</dt><dd><code>https://smartport.culltron.app</code></dd><dt>Local emulator</dt><dd><code>https://10.0.2.2:5001</code> or forwarded development HTTPS URL</dd><dt>Local device</dt><dd>Use the LAN/deployed HTTPS URL that can reach the ASP.NET app</dd></dl></article></div>
<article class="sp-card sp-download-panel"><div><span class="sp-badge sp-badge--green">Source ready</span><h2>APK availability</h2>@if(apkExists){<p>Debug APK is available for demo installation.</p><a class="sp-btn sp-btn--primary" href="/downloads/SmartPortDriverCompanion.apk">Download APK</a>}else{<p class="sp-alert sp-alert--info">Android companion source ready. Core demo works through web driver companion, WhatsApp sandbox/live-test, and mobile API.</p><p class="sp-muted">APK can be built automatically via the Android APK workflow or from Android Studio. CI uploads the debug APK artifact; copy it into <code>wwwroot/downloads</code> only when you want a web download button.</p>}</div></article>
<div class="sp-grid sp-grid--2"><article class="sp-card"><h2>Demo references</h2><p>Use one of these references in the web companion, Android app or mobile API smoke tests:</p><div class="ack-grid">@foreach(var r in refs){<code class="sp-chip">@r</code>}</div></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>Build from source</h2><ol class="sp-steps"><li>Run the GitHub Actions Android APK workflow, or open <code>mobile/SmartPortDriverCompanion</code> in Android Studio.</li><li>Set backend URL if needed; leave the default for <code>smartport.culltron.app</code>.</li><li>Build the debug APK.</li><li>Copy <code>app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk</code> to <code>src/SmartPort.Web/wwwroot/downloads/SmartPortDriverCompanion.apk</code> before deployment if you want the download button.</li><li>Install the APK on a test device and enter <code>SPQ-2026-0042</code>.</li></ol><p class="sp-muted">The Android app duplicates no backend AI logic and contains no provider tokens.</p></article></div>
